If a contract is principally for the construction or repair of improvements to real
property located in Rhode Island and the contract contains a provision that makes
the contract or any conflict arising under it subject to the law of another state;
to litigation in the courts of another state; or to arbitration in another state;
that provision is voidable by the party that is obligated by the contract to perform
the construction or repair.

(b) This chapter does not apply to a transaction to the extent it is governed by:

(1) A law governing the creation and execution of wills, codicils, or testamentary trusts; or

(2) Title 6A other than §§ 6A-1-107 and 6A-1-206, chapter 2 of title 6A, and chapter 2.1 of title 6A;

